      "message": "I think it makes the `DrawList::recordDraw` signature a little simpler if it just takes in the BarrierType and this logic is handled in `DrawContext`. \n\nThis also lets the DstContext checking `Caps`.  We can also assume that if it is an advanced blend dst usage AND not a dstReadFromInput usage that we have HW advanced blend support (but have to check whether or not a barrier is required).  If a dst read is required in the shader, no HW blending is being performed.",
